{"id":"4a7cb731de9f9107","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-df-fractal.md","title":"Fractal","display":"df-fractal — Fractal","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-fractal","aliases":["58-df-fractal","Fractal"],"display":"df-fractal — Fractal","depends_on":["[[58-df-self-similar]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-fractal"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-fractal</span><span>Fractal</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-fractal — Fractal"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"feadf4573b522982\" href=\"?note=feadf4573b522982\" title=\"58-df-self-similar\">58-df-self-similar</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\">\\(m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X=\\mathbb R^m\">\\(X=\\mathbb R^m\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d_X\\in V\">\\(d_X\\in V\\)</span> (ambient Euclidean metric graph)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\\subseteq X\">\\(F\\subseteq X\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Psi,r\\in V\">\\(\\Psi,r\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SelfSimilar}_S(F,\\Psi,r,X,d_X)\">\\(\\mathrm{SelfSimilar}_S(F,\\Psi,r,X,d_X)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"feadf4573b522982\" href=\"?note=feadf4573b522982\" title=\"58-df-self-similar\">58-df-self-similar</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> (set-function predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SelfSimilarFractal}_S(F,\\Psi,r;X,d_X)\">\\(\\mathrm{SelfSimilarFractal}_S(F,\\Psi,r;X,d_X)\\)</span> (compatibility predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}fractal} \\vdash \\mathrm{SelfSimilarFractal}_S(F,\\Psi,r;X,d_X)\\leftrightarrow\\exists m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\Bigl[X=\\mathbb R^m\\land\\mathrm{Function}(d_X,X\\times X,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\Bigl(d_X(\\langle x,y\\rangle)=\\sqrt{\\sum_{i\\in m}(x(i)-y(i))^2}\\Bigr)\\land\\mathrm{SelfSimilar}_S(F,\\Psi,r,X,d_X)\\Bigr]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}fractal} \\vdash \\mathrm{SelfSimilarFractal}_S(F,\\Psi,r;X,d_X)\\leftrightarrow\\exists m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\Bigl[X=\\mathbb R^m\\land\\mathrm{Function}(d_X,X\\times X,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\Bigl(d_X(\\langle x,y\\rangle)=\\sqrt{\\sum_{i\\in m}(x(i)-y(i))^2}\\Bigr)\\land\\mathrm{SelfSimilar}_S(F,\\Psi,r,X,d_X)\\Bigr]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This atom selects the self-similar notion of fractal, existentially binds the Euclidean dimension, and fixes the supplied metric graph to the Euclidean metric.</li>\n<li>Examples: Cantor set (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\dim_H = \\log 2 / \\log 3\">\\(\\dim_H = \\log 2 / \\log 3\\)</span>), Koch curve (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\log 4 / \\log 3\">\\(\\log 4 / \\log 3\\)</span>)</li>\n<li>Box-counting dimension: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\dim_B(F) = \\lim_{\\epsilon \\to 0} \\frac{\\log N(\\epsilon)}{\\log(1/\\epsilon)}\">\\(\\dim_B(F) = \\lim_{\\epsilon \\to 0} \\frac{\\log N(\\epsilon)}{\\log(1/\\epsilon)}\\)</span></li>\n<li>IFS (Iterated Function System): <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{F, \\psi_i\\}\">\\(\\{F, \\psi_i\\}\\)</span> determines unique fractal via fixed point</li>\n<li>Applications: natural shapes, dynamical systems, signal processing</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Falconer, Fractal Geometry</li>\n<li>Barnsley, Fractals Everywhere</li>\n<li>Hutchinson, Fractals and Self-Similarity</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-self-similar","status":"resolved","id":"feadf4573b522982","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-self-similar]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-self-similar","status":"resolved","id":"feadf4573b522982","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{SelfSimilar}_S(F,\\Psi,r,X,d_X)$ (see [[58-df-self-similar]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}","display":false},{"tex":"X=\\mathbb R^m","display":false},{"tex":"d_X\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"F\\subseteq X","display":false},{"tex":"\\Psi,r\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SelfSimilar}_S(F,\\Psi,r,X,d_X)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SelfSimilarFractal}_S(F,\\Psi,r;X,d_X)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}fractal} \\vdash \\mathrm{SelfSimilarFractal}_S(F,\\Psi,r;X,d_X)\\leftrightarrow\\exists m\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\Bigl[X=\\mathbb R^m\\land\\mathrm{Function}(d_X,X\\times X,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\Bigl(d_X(\\langle x,y\\rangle)=\\sqrt{\\sum_{i\\in m}(x(i)-y(i))^2}\\Bigr)\\land\\mathrm{SelfSimilar}_S(F,\\Psi,r,X,d_X)\\Bigr]","display":true},{"tex":"\\dim_H = \\log 2 / \\log 3","display":false},{"tex":"\\log 4 / \\log 3","display":false},{"tex":"\\dim_B(F) = \\lim_{\\epsilon \\to 0} \\frac{\\log N(\\epsilon)}{\\log(1/\\epsilon)}","display":false},{"tex":"\\{F, \\psi_i\\}","display":false}],"bytes":1611,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-548","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-fractal.md|58-df-fractal]]（batch20）"}],"outgoing":["feadf4573b522982","36d7463d215be751"]}